# Merge policy

## Trunk-based development

- `main` is the release trunk; keep it green.
- Unit/widget + Jest + governance gates run on **every PR** to `main`.
- Full Playwright E2E runs on **UAT deploy** (`release/uat-*`), not on every PR.

## Integration branch (preferred for multi-agent work)

When **one request spawns multiple agents** (or parallel feature waves), **do not commit directly to `main`**. Use:

```
main
 └── cursor/sprint-<N>-<topic>-integration-13e3   ← integration branch
      ├── cursor/<agent-a>-13e3   (disjoint file ownership)
      ├── cursor/<agent-b>-13e3
      └── single PR → main when milestone gate is met
```

**Rationale:** Cloud-agent delivery is fast; batching reduces repeated CI on `main` as test coverage grows. The human operator can coordinate spawns and minimise overlap.

**Rules:**

| Rule | Detail |
|------|--------|
| Lifetime | One sprint / one milestone; rebase on `main` before final PR |
| Merge target | Agents → **integration branch**; integration → `main` in **one PR** |
| File ownership | One agent per directory/domain; see sprint plan in `docs/refactoring-log.md` |
| Shared files | Serialise edits to `e2e/playwright/support/api.ts`, shared page objects, CI scripts |
| Verification | After each agent: confirm commits landed on the **intended** branch (`git log origin/<branch> -3`) |
| Recovery | Cherry-pick misplaced commits onto integration; do not leave orphan work |

**Direct-to-`main` PRs** remain fine for single-agent, single-domain changes that pass CI.

## Before every commit / push

1. **Sync with target branch** (`main` or integration parent):
   ```bash
   git fetch origin main
   git rebase origin/main   # or merge; resolve conflicts before push
   ```
2. Run pre-push tests (see `testing.mdc`).
3. For integration work: `node scripts/check_file_size.js` and `node e2e/scripts/check_bdd_coverage.js`.

## Branch naming (cloud agents)

- Integration: `cursor/sprint-<N>-<topic>-integration-13e3`
- Agent branches: `cursor/<descriptive-name>-13e3`

## Refactoring

- Track sprint work in `docs/refactoring-log.md`.
- One domain/screen per agent PR into integration; integration PR to `main` when sprint gate is met.
